These files make the package tests independent of the original author's
/Users/ippei directory and of network access during a test run.

The following CDISC examples are copied without content changes from
https://github.com/cdisc-org/define-xml-2.0-stylesheets
at commit e94be4ec64c3360e86d756f54533b8f4f94f8a50:

  define-adam-2.0.xml <- test/xml/define.cdisc.adam.xml
  define-arm-2.0.xml  <- test/xml/define.cdisc.arm.xml
  define-sdtm-2.0.xml <- test/xml/define.cdisc.sdtm.xml

define-sdtm-2.1.xml is copied without content changes from
https://github.com/cdisc-org/define-xml-2.1-stylesheets
at commit e54eb4821ce5dfa34598b95a6bb4c58b3618662b,
cdisc-2019/examples/DefineXML-2-1-SDTM/defineV21-SDTM.xml.
LICENSE-CDISC contains the license supplied by the stylesheet repository.

dataset-xml contains the Dataset-XML examples used by the original tests,
copied without content changes from https://github.com/VinACE/R4CDISC
at commit 6334665432b035dfddffd5fad18a01f459c0fd4d:

  R4CDISC/inst/extdata/SDTM/dm.xml
  R4CDISC/inst/extdata/SDTM/ae.xml
  R4CDISC/inst/extdata/SDTM/lb.xml
  R4CDISC/inst/extdata/SDTM/tv.xml
  R4CDISC/inst/extdata/SDTM/define2-0-0-example-sdtm(2013-11-09).xml

The last file is named dataset-xml/define.xml here. R4CDISC declares LGPL-3
in its DESCRIPTION. These examples contain CDISC demonstration data.

Two regression fixtures are derived from define-sdtm-2.0.xml. Their original
external copies were unavailable, so their intended cases are explicit:

  define-blank-descriptions.xml removes Description from IT.DM.AGE and
  IT.SC.SCORRES.MARISTAT. It empties TranslatedText for IT.DM.SEX and
  IT.VS.VSORRESU.WEIGHT.DM.COUNTRY.CMETRIC. The tests check that these four
  metadata rows remain present with missing labels.

  define-duplicate-alias.xml inserts an Alias with Context=fixture:OtherCodeID
  and Name=OTHER-CODE before the existing Alias on CL.MARISTAT and on the
  Clinical Study Sponsor EnumeratedItem. The tests check the nci:ExtCodeID
  values rather than the first alias.

The current getVarMD output adds IR_MethodOID, Controlled_Terms, Display_Value,
Permitted_Value, and Where_Condition to the original 16 columns. The SDTM 2.0
example contains 28 ordinary LB variable rows and 12 additional condition
rows. Tests assert these separately instead of treating condition rows as
additional ordinary variables.
